Founder Checklist

Microsoft Marketplace publisher

Go to 
https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/manage/createpublisher
Sign in with the Microsoft/Azure DevOps account you want to own publishing.
Create publisher:
ID: infoc-one
Name/display name: INFOC ONE
Confirm the portal accepts the ID.
Source: VS Code publishing docs say publisher ID is used in extension URLs and cannot be changed once created: 
https://code.visualstudio.com/api/working-with-extensions/publishing-extension
Azure DevOps PAT for Marketplace publishing

Go to 
https://dev.azure.com
User settings → Personal access tokens → New Token.
Organization: All accessible organizations
Scope: Custom defined → Marketplace → Manage
Store in GitHub repo secret as VSCE_PAT.
Run later: vsce login infoc-one
Open VSX namespace

Create/sign in to Eclipse account: 
https://accounts.eclipse.org
Sign publisher agreement via Open VSX account flow: 
https://open-vsx.org
Create token in Open VSX user settings.
Claim namespace:
npx ovsx create-namespace infoc-one -p <OVSX_PAT>
Store token in GitHub repo secret as OVSX_PAT.
Source: Open VSX publishing docs: 
https://github.com/eclipse-openvsx/openvsx/wiki/Publishing-Extensions
Extension slot

Check VS Marketplace URL: 
https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=infoc-one.aimeter
Check Open VSX URL: 
https://open-vsx.org/extension/infoc-one/aimeter
Both should remain empty until we publish.
GitHub

Create org: infoc-one
Create private repo: infoc-one/aimeter-infoc-one
Add repo secrets:
VSCE_PAT
OVSX_PAT
DNS

Add DNS for aimeter.infoc.one.
Use a CNAME to your static host target, or an A/AAAA record if the host requires it.
Keep it ready for the static marketing page.
Email forwarding

Create/forward:
hello@aimeter.infoc.one
support@aimeter.infoc.one
security@aimeter.infoc.one
Send test emails both directions.
